course: dictionary
lesson: 15422
title: Staggering: amazing or unsteady?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Staggering» has two meanings, and context tells you which one to use. Most often it means very surprising and shocking, because something is so large or amazing. «The number of stars in the sky is staggering.»
explain: The second meaning is a verb, the -ing form of «stagger». It means walking unsteadily, almost falling. «The boy was staggering up the hill after the long race.» Look for clues: a person, legs, or falling tell you it is the walking meaning.
explain: Ask yourself what fits. In «a staggering amount of money», a person is not walking, so the meaning is huge and amazing. Swap in a word like «huge» or «amazing» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Staggering» means very surprising and shocking, because it is so large or amazing.
fact: When it describes a number or amount, «staggering» means hugely large, as in «a staggering number».
fact: As a verb, «staggering» means walking unsteadily, almost falling, as in «the baby was staggering across the rug».
fact: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «a huge, amazing number» still makes sense, so the big-number meaning is right.
exercise: «The distance to the nearest star is staggering.» What does staggering mean here? | Cold and wet | Walking unsteadily | *Hugely large and amazing | Very small and quiet
exercise: «After the long race, Ben was staggering across the finish line.» What is Ben doing? | *Walking unsteadily, almost falling | Sitting still and calm | Running very fast | Dancing happily
exercise: «The show raised a staggering amount of money.» Find and copy the word that means very large and amazing. | money | raised | *staggering | show
test: «Her success at school was staggering.» What does staggering suggest? | *Amazing and very surprising | Quiet and sad | Slow and tired | Boring and ordinary
test: Maya reads «The baby was staggering across the rug.» What does staggering mean here? | *Walking unsteadily, almost falling | Hugely large | Happily singing | Very surprising
exam: «The price of the new car was staggering, so Dad gasped.» What does staggering mean? | *Very surprising because it is so large | Walking unsteadily | Very small | Cheap and simple
